<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-1515] IGFS: delete operations should be truly thread-safe</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1515</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-586&quot; title=&quot;[Test] GridGgfsAbstractSelfTest.testFormat() fails on TC.&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-586&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-586&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; we fixed concurrency problem in rename/move operations.&lt;br/&gt;
Since delete is actually also remove, we should fix deletion operations also accordingly using similar logic. &lt;br/&gt;
IgfsMetaManager#move0(2) method is to be used partially in delete operation &amp;#8211; need to refactor code accordingly.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
